	"notes": "Nike's homepage opens with a big wall of photos arranged like a mosaic — some wider, some narrower, not a plain grid of equal boxes — and that arrangement holds at every size tested, it just fits 2 photos per row on a phone and 4 per row on a laptop or wider. On the very widest screen the scan shows something the picture alone would not: the photo wall stops growing at about 1678 pixels and then sits pushed against the right edge of the window, so empty space builds up on the left instead of splitting evenly on both sides. On a phone the top menu shrinks to four icons — search, account, bag, and a menu button — and the full row of section links only shows up once the window is wider than about 1024 pixels. Below the photo wall, the rest of this very long page is one horizontally-scrolling product carousel after another.",
